From: AstroOS <astroos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: restack the focused view to the top of the X11 stack

wlroots 0.17+ made XWayland stacking explicit: XWM restacks every newly
mapped managed window BELOW the existing stack (xwm_handle_map_notify)
and wlr_xwayland_surface_activate() only updates _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW and
the X input focus - it never touches the stack order. Compositors are
expected to call wlr_xwayland_surface_restack() when they raise a view.
Cage 0.2.0 never does, so the X11 stack order diverges from the scene.

Xwayland delivers pointer events to the topmost X window under the
cursor (X11 XYToWindow semantics), regardless of which surface the
compositor entered. In the AstroOS kiosk every view is fullscreen at
(0,0), so when NW.js opens its DevTools window over the desktop the
DevTools view is drawn on top but sits at the bottom of the X11 stack:
every click goes to the desktop window underneath and DevTools looks
completely inert, while keyboard input (which follows the X input
focus) works.

Restack the surface to the top of the managed X11 stack whenever cage
focuses the view (map-time and click-to-focus both go through
seat_set_focus -> view_activate). Skip override-redirect surfaces:
wlroots asserts on restacking them and they manage their own stacking
(they always map above the managed windows anyway).

Mirrors sway's restack-on-focus handling of the same wlroots API.
---
diff --git a/xwayland.c b/xwayland.c
--- a/xwayland.c
+++ b/xwayland.c
@@ -83,7 +83,18 @@ static void
 activate(struct cg_view *view, bool activate)
 {
 	struct cg_xwayland_view *xwayland_view = xwayland_view_from_view(view);
-	wlr_xwayland_surface_activate(xwayland_view->xwayland_surface, activate);
+	struct wlr_xwayland_surface *xsurface = xwayland_view->xwayland_surface;
+	wlr_xwayland_surface_activate(xsurface, activate);
+
+	/* Keep the X11 stacking order in sync with the scene. Xwayland
+	 * delivers pointer events to the topmost X window under the cursor,
+	 * not to the surface with Wayland pointer focus, and XWM puts every
+	 * newly mapped managed window at the bottom of the X11 stack. Kiosk
+	 * views all cover the whole output, so unless the focused window is
+	 * raised here the views underneath keep receiving the input. */
+	if (activate && !xsurface->override_redirect) {
+		wlr_xwayland_surface_restack(xsurface, NULL, XCB_STACK_MODE_ABOVE);
+	}
 }
 
 static void
